Z||000009||Formula88||12-24-2001||09:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ok English wasnt my kind of subject, lol. Well if the movie studio gets that cut, it shouldnt even be counted in gross sales either. I cant say I 'made' $4,000 on a $4,000 job if I spent $3,000 on parts......right?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, they always refer to it as Box Office Gross, so that's correct.  That includes the money going to pay for production, star's salaries, and the studio's profits, etc.  <P>I do agree that nominating a movie before it's even out is stupid.  Unfortunately, the scenario you present of 50 people going to see a crappy nominated movie can't happen.  Why?  Because the American consumer public, by in large, are stupid sheep who are hearded wherever the advertising tells them to go.  If it's nominated, it must be good, so they'll like it, even if it sucks.<P>"The wage of sin is death.  But after taxes, you're just left with a tired feeling."<BR>||||reg||1
